<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE bindings PUBLIC "-//NetBeans//DTD Editor KeyBindings settings 1.1//EN"
                          "http://www.netbeans.org/dtds/EditorKeyBindings-1_1.dtd">
<!--
    3.2: VS Code's macOS Go Back / Go Forward, Ctrl+- and Ctrl+Shift+-, on
    the platform's own jump list (jump-list-prev / jump-list-next, the
    actions Ctrl+Left / Ctrl+Right run - chords macOS takes for switching
    desktops, so on a Mac they seldom arrive at all).

    macOS only (nbeditor-settings-targetOS=OS_MAC in the layer): O is Alt on
    Windows and Linux, where VS Code goes back with Alt+Left - which the
    platform's O-LEFT already is there.

    Registered in the NetBeans, Eclipse and NetBeans55 profiles. Measured
    in the assembled cluster: Emacs binds Ctrl+- to Collapse Fold and
    Ctrl+Shift+- to Undo, and Idea binds them to Collapse Fold and Collapse
    All Folds - a profile's own meaning of a chord wins there.
-->
<bindings>
    <bind actionName="jump-list-prev" key="O-MINUS"/>
    <bind actionName="jump-list-next" key="OS-MINUS"/>
</bindings>
